{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>עצל</b> — Everywhere it means wicked. The way of the lazy is as though hedged about with a fence of thorns, for he does not know how to get out of it." "<b>סלולה</b> — Like סולו סולו המסלה (Isaiah 62:10). Meaning: raise up, an elevation; and it hints at raised markers, so that those who walk on it do not go astray. And likewise סוללה: as though it has raised markers to go in a straight path."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:01.550650845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}